{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/540793-rites-du-cheval-variation","id":540793,"title":"Rites Du Cheval variation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-05T02:50:58-07:00","id":540793,"title":"Rites Du Cheval variation","content":"Hello. After reading Pact Magic from Pathfinder, I'm thinking in retooling Les Mysteres' endowment into something similar, more versatile than the original yet a bit more dangerous for the &quot;horse&quot;. <br /> Also I would like to use the Loa as vestiges, maybe thought a voodoo ceremony where the hougan or mambo allow the hunter to be ridden by the god. Any ideas regarding the mechanics?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T00:00:15-07:00","id":542333,"title":"","content":"An alternate route for Les Mysteres powers are always welcome.<br /> <br /> As a Vestige I think having the Hunter swear fealty to a particular Spirit with an assortment of bonuses tied to it that increase as the character gains dots in the Endowment would fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T09:25:16-07:00","id":542684,"title":"","content":"To be honest, I didn't understand (neither the book is clear about) how the rites works: are they like Gifts, so the hunter may use them in any moment, or must he/she perform a ceremony and be possesed by a spirit each time ? How many adquired rites can be used, and how many times?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T07:04:44-07:00","id":734615,"title":"","content":"I think the best reference for redefining the Rites du Cheval would be the mechanics for rites in Werewolf the Forsaken: Second Edition. Especially since the system encourages individual players who use ritual magic to conceptualize their personal rites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T07:13:50-07:00","id":734623,"title":"","content":"I think the best reference for redefining the Rites du Cheval would be the mechanics for rites in Werewolf the Forsaken: Second Edition. Especially since it would further reinforce how different (yet similar) they are to the Uratha. Also, the system encourages individual players who use ritual magic to conceptualize their personal rites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T09:45:46-07:00","id":744631,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I mean, there is actually a werewolf rite that does pretty much exactly what the rites of cheval do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 10-31-2015, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T11:08:27-07:00","id":744716,"title":"","content":"Mmmm... maybe. But I have been looking also to <a href=\"http://hunter-the-vigil-cults.wikia.com/wiki/Chapter_Four:_Theology\" target=\"_blank\">http://hunter-the-vigil-cults.wikia....Four:_Theology</a>. It would be easy to take the adapt the Avatar mechanic with the Loa (Samedi, Ghede, Erzulie) .<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T23:38:18-08:00","id":750781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/540793-rites-du-cheval-variation?p=744716#post744716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mmmm... maybe. But I have been looking also to <a href=\"http://hunter-the-vigil-cults.wikia.com/wiki/Chapter_Four:_Theology\" target=\"_blank\">http://hunter-the-vigil-cults.wikia....Four:_Theology</a>. It would be easy to take the adapt the Avatar mechanic with the Loa (Samedi, Ghede, Erzulie) .<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Whoa. I'm definitely bookmarking that link. But yeah, I can see how the Avatar mechanics would work as a possible framework for redesigning the Rites du Cheval. Though perhaps you can use whatever rendition you make of it alongside a system of ritual magic based on 2E Werewolf Rites? On a sidenote, I skimmed some of the Endowments on that page, and they look promising for inclusion into my stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T03:03:53-08:00","id":751014,"title":"","content":"In the Werewolf 2 ed corebook, is noted sometimes Urathas find Cults of vanilla humans whom are able to practice rites, usually by bounding themselves with some spirit patron. Maybe <i>Du Cheval </i>treats the loa (or the spirits who pretend to be loas) as Totems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}